## Idea 4 Gold Float
- Axis Bank + Freecharge (Freecharge = 100% Axis sub) launched gold-backed credit on UPI 29 Sep 2025, pay interest on used amount, existing Axis customers, MSME focus, NPCI secured credit-line framework. https://www.axis.bank.in/about-us/press-releases/axis-bank-launches-indias-first-gold-backed-credit-on-upi-powered-by-freecharge
- UPI credit lines: banks + SFBs only (extended to SFBs Dec 2024); NBFCs not permitted (2023 analysis; no evidence added since). https://mondaq.com/india/financial-services/1365422/rbis-upi-expansion-with-credit-lines
- The Ken: RBI wants to stop most NBFCs offering revolving credit https://the-ken.com/story/the-rbis-revolving-credit-rule-treats-every-nbfc-like-a-bad-lender/
- Bullet consumption <=12m; renewals/top-ups only after accrued interest paid. No explicit revolving permission found.
- Addressable = bank gold book (INR5.1 lakh cr ~ $55B), not 9.03cr accounts. Verdict KILL. median $2M upside $25M.

## Idea 5 Switch Desk
- Lender-run balance transfer exists: Shriram, L&T Finance, Bajaj, IIFL FAQ pages. https://www.shriramfinance.in/financial-faq-how-can-i-apply-for-a-gold-loan-balance-transfer ; https://www.ltfinance.com/blog/gold-loan/gold-loan-transfer
- Rate gap real but < pitch: Muthoot ~16.3%, Manappuram ~16.6%, IIFL/Capri ~18.6% vs SBI ~9.6% (gap ~7-9 pts not 10-20). Muthoot guided FY26 NIM peak, normalising. Banks' retail gold +105% y/y to INR5.1 lakh cr (May 2026) w/o a desk.
- Bank LTV lower (65%) per Shriram FAQ => switching to bank often cuts loan amount.
- Verdict weak. median $6M upside $50M (banks' disbursal INR ~6-7 lakh cr/yr x 15% x 0.5% = ~$57M).

